</aside>

		<div class="content-body">
			<main>
				<a id="top"></a>
				<div id="siteNotice"></div>
				<div class="mw-indicators">
				</div>
				<h1 id="firstHeading" class="firstHeading mw-first-heading"><span class="mw-page-title-main">Mechanics</span></h1>
				<div id="bodyContent" class="vector-body">
					<div id="siteSub" class="noprint">From Slay the Spire Wiki</div>
					<div id="contentSub"></div>
					<div id="contentSub2"></div>
					
					<div id="jump-to-nav"></div>
					<a class="mw-jump-link" href="#mw-head">Jump to navigation</a>
					<a class="mw-jump-link" href="#searchInput">Jump to search</a>
					<div id="mw-content-text" class="mw-body-content"><div class="mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output" lang="en" dir="ltr"><div class="game-tabber noexcerpt"><div class="game-tab" style="border: 2px solid var(--wiki-accent-color--hover); border-bottom: none;"><a class="mw-selflink selflink">Slay the Spire</a></div> <div class="game-tab"><a href="/wiki/Slay_the_Spire_2:Mechanics" title="Slay the Spire 2:Mechanics">Slay the Spire 2</a></div></div>
<div class="ambox" style="--ambox-color: red;"><div class="ambox-icon metadata"><img alt="" src="/images/thumb/GremlinNob.png/42px-GremlinNob.png?deef85" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="42" height="48" srcset="/images/thumb/GremlinNob.png/62px-GremlinNob.png?deef85 1.5x, /images/thumb/GremlinNob.png/83px-GremlinNob.png?deef85 2x" data-file-width="433" data-file-height="499" /></div><div class="ambox-content"><p class="ambox-title">WARNING!</p><p class="ambox-text"><i>This page is under construction. Information may be wrong or incomplete.</i></p></div></div>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Resources">Resources</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?veaction=edit&amp;section=1" title="Edit section: Resources" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?action=edit&amp;section=1" title="Edit section&#039;s source code: Resources"><span>edit source</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h2>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Health">Health</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?veaction=edit&amp;section=2" title="Edit section: Health" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?action=edit&amp;section=2" title="Edit section&#039;s source code: Health"><span>edit source</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<blockquote> <p><i><b>Hit Points (HP):</b> If you run out of HP, you die.</i></p></blockquote>
<p>The most fundamental resource. HP can take any value from 0 to the player's maximum HP. HP is depleted by taking damage, and may be replenished at <a href="/wiki/Map_Locations#Rest_Sites" title="Map Locations">Rest Sites</a>, between acts, or with any number of healing effects.
</p><p>Max HP can be raised or lowered by various cards, relics, and events. Increasing max HP will also increase your current HP by the same amount.
</p><p>Read more about <a href="/wiki/Health" title="Health">Health</a>.
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Cards">Cards</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?veaction=edit&amp;section=3" title="Edit section: Cards" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?action=edit&amp;section=3" title="Edit section&#039;s source code: Cards"><span>edit source</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<p>Each character comes equipped with a starting deck of 10 or 12 cards. Cards are played during combat. 
</p><p>Outside of combat, they may be added, removed, upgraded, or transformed. Some cards or relics can also upgrade cards mid combat.
</p><p>Read more about <a href="/wiki/Cards" title="Cards">Cards</a>.
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Upgrading">Upgrading</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?veaction=edit&amp;section=4" title="Edit section: Upgrading" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?action=edit&amp;section=4" title="Edit section&#039;s source code: Upgrading"><span>edit source</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<blockquote><p><i>Upgrading cards makes them more powerful. Cards can only be upgraded once.</i></p></blockquote>
<p>Read more about <a href="/wiki/Upgrade" title="Upgrade">Upgrade</a>.
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Transforming">Transforming</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?veaction=edit&amp;section=5" title="Edit section: Transforming" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?action=edit&amp;section=5" title="Edit section&#039;s source code: Transforming"><span>edit source</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<blockquote><p><i>Transformed cards become a random card of any rarity.</i></p></blockquote>
<p>Read more about <a href="/wiki/Transform" title="Transform">Transform rules</a>.
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Gold">Gold</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?veaction=edit&amp;section=6" title="Edit section: Gold" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?action=edit&amp;section=6" title="Edit section&#039;s source code: Gold"><span>edit source</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<blockquote> <p><i><b>Money Pouch:</b> Shows how much gold you're carrying. Gold is the currency within the Spire.</i></p></blockquote>
<p>Obtained from combat rewards, <a href="/wiki/Events" title="Events">Events</a>, <a href="/wiki/Chests" class="mw-redirect" title="Chests">Chests</a> and certain relics/cards. Can be spent at the <a href="/wiki/Merchant" class="mw-redirect" title="Merchant">Merchant</a> and certain <a href="/wiki/Events" title="Events">Events</a> to make purchases.
</p><p>Read more about <a href="/wiki/Gold" title="Gold">Gold</a>.
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Potions">Potions</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?veaction=edit&amp;section=7" title="Edit section: Potions" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?action=edit&amp;section=7" title="Edit section&#039;s source code: Potions"><span>edit source</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<blockquote> <p><i>Use potions during combat to gain bonuses or hinder enemies.</i></p></blockquote><p>Single-use consumables that persist across combats.
</p><p>Read more about <a href="/wiki/Potions" title="Potions">Potions</a>.
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Keys">Keys</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?veaction=edit&amp;section=8" title="Edit section: Keys" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?action=edit&amp;section=8" title="Edit section&#039;s source code: Keys"><span>edit source</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<p>After a run has been won on <a href="/wiki/Ironclad" title="Ironclad">Ironclad</a>, <a href="/wiki/Silent" title="Silent">Silent</a> and <a href="/wiki/Defect" title="Defect">Defect</a>, an icon of 3 empty <b>Keys</b> appear to the left of the player's name. To access <a href="/wiki/Acts#Act_4:_The_Ending" title="Acts">Act 4</a>, all 3 <b>Keys</b> need to be collected in the same run. They do not have to be collected in the same Act.
</p>
<ul><li><a href="/wiki/File:Ruby_Key.png" class="image"><img alt="Ruby Key.png" src="/images/thumb/Ruby_Key.png/40px-Ruby_Key.png?8088f3" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="40" height="32" srcset="/images/Ruby_Key.png?8088f3 1.5x" data-file-width="54" data-file-height="43" /></a> <span class="ironclad-text"><b>Ruby Key</b></span>: Can be obtained at a Rest Site by clicking the <b>Recall</b> action, instead of Smith or Rest (or <span class="relic-trigger inline-trigger" data-name="Girya" data-sequel="1"><a href="/wiki/Girya" title="Girya"><img alt="Girya.png" src="/images/thumb/Girya.png/24px-Girya.png?44e44f" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="24" height="24" style="vertical-align: middle" srcset="/images/thumb/Girya.png/36px-Girya.png?44e44f 1.5x, /images/thumb/Girya.png/48px-Girya.png?44e44f 2x" data-file-width="156" data-file-height="156" /></a> <a href="/wiki/Girya" title="Girya">Lift</a></span>, <span class="relic-trigger inline-trigger" data-name="Shovel" data-sequel="1"><a href="/wiki/Shovel" title="Shovel"><img alt="Shovel.png" src="/images/thumb/Shovel.png/24px-Shovel.png?2ddcce" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="24" height="24" style="vertical-align: middle" srcset="/images/thumb/Shovel.png/36px-Shovel.png?2ddcce 1.5x, /images/thumb/Shovel.png/48px-Shovel.png?2ddcce 2x" data-file-width="156" data-file-height="156" /></a> <a href="/wiki/Shovel" title="Shovel">Dig</a></span> and <span class="relic-trigger inline-trigger" data-name="Peace Pipe" data-sequel="1"><a href="/wiki/Peace_Pipe" title="Peace Pipe"><img alt="PeacePipe.png" src="/images/thumb/PeacePipe.png/24px-PeacePipe.png?9c5737" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="24" height="24" style="vertical-align: middle" srcset="/images/thumb/PeacePipe.png/36px-PeacePipe.png?9c5737 1.5x, /images/thumb/PeacePipe.png/48px-PeacePipe.png?9c5737 2x" data-file-width="156" data-file-height="156" /></a> <a href="/wiki/Peace_Pipe" title="Peace Pipe">Toke</a></span>) at the same fire.</li></ul>
<ul><li><a href="/wiki/File:Emerald_Key.png" class="image"><img alt="Emerald Key.png" src="/images/thumb/Emerald_Key.png/30px-Emerald_Key.png?ba33e5" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="30" height="43" srcset="/images/Emerald_Key.png?ba33e5 1.5x" data-file-width="40" data-file-height="57" /></a> <span class="silent-text"><b>Emerald Key</b></span>: Can be obtained by fighting a "super" elite, indicated by a burning animation on a map. Once the Emerald Key is obtained, super elites won't show up in later Acts.</li></ul>
<ul><li><a href="/wiki/File:Sapphire_Key.png" class="image"><img alt="Sapphire Key.png" src="/images/thumb/Sapphire_Key.png/40px-Sapphire_Key.png?92386e" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="40" height="32" srcset="/images/Sapphire_Key.png?92386e 1.5x" data-file-width="53" data-file-height="43" /></a> <span class="defect-text"><b>Sapphire Key</b></span>: Can be obtained at any Chest instead of the Relic in the chest. Will not appear if <span class="relic-trigger inline-trigger" data-name="N&#39;loth&#39;s Hungry Face" data-sequel="1"><a href="/wiki/N%27loth%27s_Hungry_Face" title="N&#39;loth&#39;s Hungry Face"><img alt="NlothsMask.png" src="/images/thumb/NlothsMask.png/24px-NlothsMask.png?420bdb" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="24" height="24" style="vertical-align: middle" srcset="/images/thumb/NlothsMask.png/36px-NlothsMask.png?420bdb 1.5x, /images/thumb/NlothsMask.png/48px-NlothsMask.png?420bdb 2x" data-file-width="156" data-file-height="156" /></a> <a href="/wiki/N%27loth%27s_Hungry_Face" title="N&#39;loth&#39;s Hungry Face">N'loth's Hungry Face</a></span> is active. Will only be linked to the bottom Relic if <span class="relic-trigger inline-trigger" data-name="Matryoshka" data-sequel="1"><a href="/wiki/Matryoshka" title="Matryoshka"><img alt="Matryoshka.png" src="/images/thumb/Matryoshka.png/24px-Matryoshka.png?5adf8f" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="24" height="24" style="vertical-align: middle" srcset="/images/thumb/Matryoshka.png/36px-Matryoshka.png?5adf8f 1.5x, /images/thumb/Matryoshka.png/48px-Matryoshka.png?5adf8f 2x" data-file-width="156" data-file-height="156" /></a> <a href="/wiki/Matryoshka" title="Matryoshka">Matryoshka</a></span> is active.</li></ul>
<p><b>Trivia:</b> These three keys appear in the game <a class="external text" href="https://deadcells.wiki.gg/">Dead Cells</a> and unlock an <a class="external text" href="https://deadcells.wiki.gg/wiki/Outfits#Ironclad_Outfit">outfit</a> resembling the <a href="/wiki/Ironclad" title="Ironclad">Ironclad</a>.
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="In_Combat">In Combat</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?veaction=edit&amp;section=9" title="Edit section: In Combat" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?action=edit&amp;section=9" title="Edit section&#039;s source code: In Combat"><span>edit source</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h2>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Card_Piles">Card Piles</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?veaction=edit&amp;section=10" title="Edit section: Card Piles" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?action=edit&amp;section=10" title="Edit section&#039;s source code: Card Piles"><span>edit source</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<p>There are three piles in which cards may reside when not in the player's hand.
</p>
<ul><li><b>Draw Pile</b>: The pile from which cards are drawn at the start of the turn. The draw pile is populated at the start of combat with all the cards from the player's deck. Attempting to draw a card when the draw pile is empty triggers a shuffle (see below).</li>
<li><b>Discard Pile</b>: The pile to which most cards are sent after playing. When a shuffle is triggered, all cards from the discard pile are shuffled into the draw pile. Certain cards do not enter the discard pile after being played: <a href="/wiki/Exhaust" title="Exhaust">Exhaust</a> cards instead enter the exhaust pile, while <span class="plainlink" data-name="Cards"><a class="text" href="https://slaythespire.wiki.gg/wiki/Cards_List?type=Power"><span>Powers</span></a></span> cards disappear entirely.</li>
<li><b>Exhaust Pile</b>: The pile in which cards that have been <a href="/wiki/Exhaust" title="Exhaust">Exhausted</a> reside. There is no way to recover cards from this pile, except with <span class="card-trigger inline-trigger" data-name="Exhume" data-sequel="1"><a href="/wiki/Exhume" title="Exhume"><img alt="CardIcon Ironclad Skill Rare.png" src="/images/thumb/CardIcon_Ironclad_Skill_Rare.png/24px-CardIcon_Ironclad_Skill_Rare.png?78fe01" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="24" height="24" style="vertical-align: middle" srcset="/images/CardIcon_Ironclad_Skill_Rare.png?78fe01 1.5x" data-file-width="32" data-file-height="32" /></a> <a href="/wiki/Exhume" title="Exhume">Exhume</a></span>.</li></ul>
<p>Certain enemies have attacks that shuffle <span class="plainlink" data-name="Cards"><a class="text" href="https://slaythespire.wiki.gg/wiki/Cards_List?type=Status"><span>Status</span></a></span> cards into the discard or draw piles. Player cards may also shuffle cards into the discard pile (e.g. <span class="card-trigger inline-trigger" data-name="Overclock" data-sequel="1"><a href="/wiki/Overclock" title="Overclock"><img alt="CardIcon Defect Skill Uncommon.png" src="/images/thumb/CardIcon_Defect_Skill_Uncommon.png/24px-CardIcon_Defect_Skill_Uncommon.png?12d106" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="24" height="24" style="vertical-align: middle" srcset="/images/CardIcon_Defect_Skill_Uncommon.png?12d106 1.5x" data-file-width="32" data-file-height="32" /></a> <a href="/wiki/Overclock" title="Overclock">Overclock</a></span>) or draw pile (e.g. <span class="card-trigger inline-trigger" data-name="Alpha" data-sequel="1"><a href="/wiki/Alpha" title="Alpha"><img alt="CardIcon Watcher Skill Rare.png" src="/images/thumb/CardIcon_Watcher_Skill_Rare.png/24px-CardIcon_Watcher_Skill_Rare.png?ae356d" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="24" height="24" style="vertical-align: middle" srcset="/images/CardIcon_Watcher_Skill_Rare.png?ae356d 1.5x" data-file-width="32" data-file-height="32" /></a> <a href="/wiki/Alpha" title="Alpha">Alpha</a></span>).
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Hand">Hand</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?veaction=edit&amp;section=11" title="Edit section: Hand" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?action=edit&amp;section=11" title="Edit section&#039;s source code: Hand"><span>edit source</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<p>The hand is where cards reside after drawing and before playing. During their turn, players may play cards from the hand, so long as they have the <span class="keyword-trigger inline-trigger" data-name="Energy" data-sequel="1" title=""><a href="/wiki/Keywords#Energy" title="Keywords"><img alt="ColorlessEnergy.png" src="/images/thumb/ColorlessEnergy.png/18px-ColorlessEnergy.png?259ded" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="18" height="18" srcset="/images/thumb/ColorlessEnergy.png/27px-ColorlessEnergy.png?259ded 1.5x, /images/thumb/ColorlessEnergy.png/36px-ColorlessEnergy.png?259ded 2x" data-file-width="164" data-file-height="164" /></a> <a href="/wiki/Keywords#Energy" title="Keywords">Energy</a></span> to do so.
</p>
<h4><span class="mw-headline" id="Hand_Size_Limit">Hand Size Limit</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?veaction=edit&amp;section=12" title="Edit section: Hand Size Limit" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?action=edit&amp;section=12" title="Edit section&#039;s source code: Hand Size Limit"><span>edit source</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h4>
<p>The maximum number of cards allowed in hand is 10. There is no way to exceed this limit. Any draw action that would result in more than 10 cards in the player's hand will result in the remaining cards entering the discard pile immediately. Similarly, anything that creates cards, whether a relic (e.g. <span class="relic-trigger inline-trigger" data-name="Dead Branch" data-sequel="1"><a href="/wiki/Dead_Branch" title="Dead Branch"><img alt="DeadBranch.png" src="/images/thumb/DeadBranch.png/24px-DeadBranch.png?b0e6b0" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="24" height="24" style="vertical-align: middle" srcset="/images/thumb/DeadBranch.png/36px-DeadBranch.png?b0e6b0 1.5x, /images/thumb/DeadBranch.png/48px-DeadBranch.png?b0e6b0 2x" data-file-width="156" data-file-height="156" /></a> <a href="/wiki/Dead_Branch" title="Dead Branch">Dead Branch</a></span>) or another card (e.g. <span class="card-trigger inline-trigger" data-name="Blade Dance" data-sequel="1"><a href="/wiki/Blade_Dance" title="Blade Dance"><img alt="CardIcon Silent Skill Common.png" src="/images/thumb/CardIcon_Silent_Skill_Common.png/24px-CardIcon_Silent_Skill_Common.png?711671" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="24" height="24" style="vertical-align: middle" srcset="/images/CardIcon_Silent_Skill_Common.png?711671 1.5x" data-file-width="32" data-file-height="32" /></a> <a href="/wiki/Blade_Dance" title="Blade Dance">Blade Dance</a></span>), will send excess cards to the draw pile, so that the hand size limit is maintained at all times.
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Turns">Turns</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?veaction=edit&amp;section=13" title="Edit section: Turns" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?action=edit&amp;section=13" title="Edit section&#039;s source code: Turns"><span>edit source</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<p>Combat is turn-based: first the player takes a turn, then the enemy party takes a turn, then repeat. This continues until either the enemy or the player dies.
</p>
<h4><span class="mw-headline" id="Player_Turn">Player Turn</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?veaction=edit&amp;section=14" title="Edit section: Player Turn" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?action=edit&amp;section=14" title="Edit section&#039;s source code: Player Turn"><span>edit source</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h4>
<p>At the start of the player's turn, three things happen:
</p>
<ol><li>Energy is set to the base energy (default 3), and</li>
<li>A number of cards are drawn (default 5), and</li>
<li>Start-of-turn effects trigger.</li></ol>
<p>The default behavior can be changed, typically by <a href="/wiki/Relics" title="Relics">Relics</a> (e.g. <span class="relic-trigger inline-trigger" data-name="Fusion Hammer" data-sequel="1"><a href="/wiki/Fusion_Hammer" title="Fusion Hammer"><img alt="FusionHammer.png" src="/images/thumb/FusionHammer.png/24px-FusionHammer.png?e0e3b2" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="24" height="24" style="vertical-align: middle" srcset="/images/thumb/FusionHammer.png/36px-FusionHammer.png?e0e3b2 1.5x, /images/thumb/FusionHammer.png/48px-FusionHammer.png?e0e3b2 2x" data-file-width="156" data-file-height="156" /></a> <a href="/wiki/Fusion_Hammer" title="Fusion Hammer">Fusion Hammer</a></span> increases the base energy by 1; <span class="relic-trigger inline-trigger" data-name="Snecko Eye" data-sequel="1"><a href="/wiki/Snecko_Eye" title="Snecko Eye"><img alt="SneckoEye.png" src="/images/thumb/SneckoEye.png/24px-SneckoEye.png?9be98a" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="24" height="24" style="vertical-align: middle" srcset="/images/thumb/SneckoEye.png/36px-SneckoEye.png?9be98a 1.5x, /images/thumb/SneckoEye.png/48px-SneckoEye.png?9be98a 2x" data-file-width="156" data-file-height="156" /></a> <a href="/wiki/Snecko_Eye" title="Snecko Eye">Snecko Eye</a></span> increases the number of cards drawn per turn by 2).
</p><p>During their turn, the player may play cards or drink <a href="/wiki/Potions" title="Potions">Potions</a>. Cards with an energy cost will subtract that energy from the total. All player actions are resolved immediately upon being performed.
</p><p>When the player presses End Turn, two things happen:
</p>
<ol><li>End-of-turn effects trigger.
<ul><li>This generally resolves in the order <b>relics -&gt; buffs -&gt; cards</b> (e.g. <span class="relic-trigger inline-trigger" data-name="Orichalcum" data-sequel="1"><a href="/wiki/Orichalcum" title="Orichalcum"><img alt="Orichalcum.png" src="/images/thumb/Orichalcum.png/24px-Orichalcum.png?c37c55" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="24" height="24" style="vertical-align: middle" srcset="/images/thumb/Orichalcum.png/36px-Orichalcum.png?c37c55 1.5x, /images/thumb/Orichalcum.png/48px-Orichalcum.png?c37c55 2x" data-file-width="156" data-file-height="156" /></a> <a href="/wiki/Orichalcum" title="Orichalcum">Orichalcum</a></span> will trigger before <span class="power-trigger inline-trigger" data-name="Plated Armor" data-sequel="1"><a href="/wiki/Plated_Armor" title="Plated Armor"><img alt="Icon PlatedArmor.png" src="/images/thumb/Icon_PlatedArmor.png/22px-Icon_PlatedArmor.png?647bdc" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="22" height="22" srcset="/images/thumb/Icon_PlatedArmor.png/33px-Icon_PlatedArmor.png?647bdc 1.5x, /images/thumb/Icon_PlatedArmor.png/44px-Icon_PlatedArmor.png?647bdc 2x" data-file-width="109" data-file-height="109" /></a> <a href="/wiki/Plated_Armor" title="Plated Armor">Plated Armor</a></span>, which will trigger before <span class="card-trigger inline-trigger" data-name="Burn" data-sequel="1"><a href="/wiki/Burn" title="Burn"><img alt="CardIcon Status.png" src="/images/thumb/CardIcon_Status.png/24px-CardIcon_Status.png?5935a6" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="24" height="24" style="vertical-align: middle" srcset="/images/CardIcon_Status.png?5935a6 1.5x" data-file-width="32" data-file-height="32" /></a> <a href="/wiki/Burn" title="Burn">Burns</a></span>).</li></ul></li>
<li>Cards in hand are shuffled into the discard pile.
<ul><li>This will not occur with <span class="relic-trigger inline-trigger" data-name="Runic Pyramid" data-sequel="1"><a href="/wiki/Runic_Pyramid" title="Runic Pyramid"><img alt="RunicPyramid.png" src="/images/thumb/RunicPyramid.png/24px-RunicPyramid.png?b3c035" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="24" height="24" style="vertical-align: middle" srcset="/images/thumb/RunicPyramid.png/36px-RunicPyramid.png?b3c035 1.5x, /images/thumb/RunicPyramid.png/48px-RunicPyramid.png?b3c035 2x" data-file-width="156" data-file-height="156" /></a> <a href="/wiki/Runic_Pyramid" title="Runic Pyramid">Runic Pyramid</a></span> or any cards that are <span class="keyword-trigger inline-trigger" data-name="Retain" data-sequel="1" title=""><a href="/wiki/Keywords#Retain" title="Keywords">Retained</a></span>, unless they are cards with end-of-turn Effects like <span class="card-trigger inline-trigger" data-name="Regret" data-sequel="1"><a href="/wiki/Regret" title="Regret"><img alt="CardIcon Curse.png" src="/images/thumb/CardIcon_Curse.png/24px-CardIcon_Curse.png?f11a8c" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="24" height="24" style="vertical-align: middle" srcset="/images/CardIcon_Curse.png?f11a8c 1.5x" data-file-width="32" data-file-height="32" /></a> <a href="/wiki/Regret" title="Regret">Regret</a></span> or <span class="card-trigger inline-trigger" data-name="Burn" data-sequel="1"><a href="/wiki/Burn" title="Burn"><img alt="CardIcon Status.png" src="/images/thumb/CardIcon_Status.png/24px-CardIcon_Status.png?5935a6" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="24" height="24" style="vertical-align: middle" srcset="/images/CardIcon_Status.png?5935a6 1.5x" data-file-width="32" data-file-height="32" /></a> <a href="/wiki/Burn" title="Burn">Burn</a></span>.
<ul><li>Cards with end-of-turn Effects can sometimes also be <span class="keyword-trigger inline-trigger" data-name="Retain" data-sequel="1" title=""><a href="/wiki/Keywords#Retain" title="Keywords">Retained</a></span> at exactly 1 point: during the <span class="enemy-trigger inline-trigger" data-name="Awakened One" data-sequel="1"><a href="/wiki/Awakened_One#Awakened_One" title="Awakened One"><img alt="Map-Awakened.png" src="/images/thumb/Map-Awakened.png/22px-Map-Awakened.png?bfea9f" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="22" height="22" style="vertical-align: middle" srcset="/images/thumb/Map-Awakened.png/33px-Map-Awakened.png?bfea9f 1.5x, /images/thumb/Map-Awakened.png/44px-Map-Awakened.png?bfea9f 2x" data-file-width="512" data-file-height="512" /></a> <a href="/wiki/Awakened_One#Awakened_One" title="Awakened One">Awakened One</a></span> phase shift. If Awakened One's first phase is killed with an effect that takes place right after the player's turn ends, but before the enemy turn begins (Defect's <span class="keyword-trigger" data-name="@LO" data-sequel="1"><img alt="LightningOrb.png" src="/images/thumb/LightningOrb.png/24px-LightningOrb.png?295517" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="24" height="24" style="vertical-align: middle" srcset="/images/thumb/LightningOrb.png/36px-LightningOrb.png?295517 1.5x, /images/thumb/LightningOrb.png/48px-LightningOrb.png?295517 2x" data-file-width="70" data-file-height="70" /></span> Lightning Orb passive or <span class="relic-trigger inline-trigger" data-name="Stone Calendar" data-sequel="1"><a href="/wiki/Stone_Calendar" title="Stone Calendar"><img alt="StoneCalendar.png" src="/images/thumb/StoneCalendar.png/24px-StoneCalendar.png?23e7f8" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="24" height="24" style="vertical-align: middle" srcset="/images/thumb/StoneCalendar.png/36px-StoneCalendar.png?23e7f8 1.5x, /images/thumb/StoneCalendar.png/48px-StoneCalendar.png?23e7f8 2x" data-file-width="156" data-file-height="156" /></a> <a href="/wiki/Stone_Calendar" title="Stone Calendar">Stone Calendar</a></span>), cards that would normally be discarded like <span class="card-trigger inline-trigger" data-name="Burn" data-sequel="1"><a href="/wiki/Burn" title="Burn"><img alt="CardIcon Status.png" src="/images/thumb/CardIcon_Status.png/24px-CardIcon_Status.png?5935a6" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="24" height="24" style="vertical-align: middle" srcset="/images/CardIcon_Status.png?5935a6 1.5x" data-file-width="32" data-file-height="32" /></a> <a href="/wiki/Burn" title="Burn">Burn</a></span> can be <span class="keyword-trigger inline-trigger" data-name="Retain" data-sequel="1" title=""><a href="/wiki/Keywords#Retain" title="Keywords">Retained</a></span>.</li></ul></li></ul></li></ol>
<p>Then the enemy party takes its turn.
</p>
<h4><span class="mw-headline" id="Enemy_Turn">Enemy Turn</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?veaction=edit&amp;section=15" title="Edit section: Enemy Turn" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?action=edit&amp;section=15" title="Edit section&#039;s source code: Enemy Turn"><span>edit source</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h4>
<p>Enemy actions during their turn are governed by their <a href="/wiki/Intent" title="Intent">Intents</a>, visible as floating symbols above their heads. In multi-enemy encounters, enemies always take actions from left to right.
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Outside_Combat">Outside Combat</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?veaction=edit&amp;section=16" title="Edit section: Outside Combat" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?action=edit&amp;section=16" title="Edit section&#039;s source code: Outside Combat"><span>edit source</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h2>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Acts">Acts</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?veaction=edit&amp;section=17" title="Edit section: Acts" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?action=edit&amp;section=17" title="Edit section&#039;s source code: Acts"><span>edit source</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<p>Slay the Spire is split up into 3 acts: <a href="/wiki/Acts#Act_1:_Exordium" title="Acts">The Exordium</a>, <a href="/wiki/Acts#Act_2:_The_City" title="Acts">The City</a>, and <a href="/wiki/Acts#Act_3:_The_Beyond" title="Acts">The Beyond</a>. Each act is 17 floors long and has certain features in common, such as a <a href="/wiki/Boss" class="mw-redirect" title="Boss">Boss</a> encounter at the end. An optional fourth act, <a href="/wiki/Acts#Act_4:_The_Ending" title="Acts">The Ending</a>, is unlocked after beating the game once with each of <a href="/wiki/Ironclad" title="Ironclad">Ironclad</a>, <a href="/wiki/Silent" title="Silent">Silent</a>, and <a href="/wiki/Defect" title="Defect">Defect</a> (see <a href="#Keys">Keys</a>).
</p><p>Read more about <a href="/wiki/Acts" title="Acts">Acts</a>.
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Floors_and_Floor_Types">Floors and Floor Types</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?veaction=edit&amp;section=18" title="Edit section: Floors and Floor Types" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?action=edit&amp;section=18" title="Edit section&#039;s source code: Floors and Floor Types"><span>edit source</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3>
<p>After completing any mandatory objectives, such as defeating enemies or choosing an option at an <a href="/wiki/Event" class="mw-redirect" title="Event">Event</a>, the player may proceed to the next floor using the Map interface. Only floors ("nodes") that are connected to the current floor with a dotted line on the map can be accessed. Each floor may be one of seven different types.
</p><p>Read more about <a href="/wiki/Map_Locations" title="Map Locations">Map Locations</a>.
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Chests">Chests</span><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?veaction=edit&amp;section=19" title="Edit section: Chests" class="mw-editsection-visualeditor"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-divider"> | </span><a href="/wiki/Mechanics?action=edit&amp;section=19" title="Edit section&#039;s source code: Chests"><span>edit source</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></h3><div class="hatnote">See <a href="/wiki/Map_Locations" title="Map Locations">Map Locations</a> for all possible rooms.</div>
<p>Chests are objects which contain some amount of Gold and a <a href="/wiki/Relic" class="mw-redirect" title="Relic">Relic</a>. Chests are only obtained through killing <a href="/wiki/Bosses" title="Bosses">bosses</a>, or encountering <a href="/wiki/Treasure_Rooms" class="mw-redirect" title="Treasure Rooms">Treasure Rooms</a>. 
</p><p>Boss Chests offer a choice of three different <span class="plainlink" data-name="Relics"><a class="text" href="https://slaythespire.wiki.gg/wiki/Relics_List?rarity=Boss"><span>Boss Relics</span></a></span>. You can choose to skip this reward. 
</p><p>There are three types of Non-Boss chests: Small, Medium and Large. Each has a different chance to give you a <a href="/wiki/Relic" class="mw-redirect" title="Relic">Relic</a> and some amount of <a href="/wiki/Gold" title="Gold">Gold</a>.
</p>
